An attacker tampers with cookies to set logged_in=1 without authenticating. Which statement is the most accurate?', '["The system is vulnerable \u2014 cookie-only checks bypass server session validation", "The system is secure \u2014 session data cannot be forged without the server-side secret", "The system is vulnerable only if session_id is exposed", "The system is secure if HTTPS is used,"]', 'The system is vulnerable — cookie-only checks bypass server session validation.', 'The server-side session ($_SESSION[''user_id'']) is secure — it''s stored on the server and tied to a session ID. However, if the application ALSO checks a client-side cookie (logged_in=1) to decide if a user is authenticated, an attacker can simply set that cookie to 1 in their browser without ever logging in. The server-side session is never actually verified. Always rely solely on server-side session data for authentication checks.', 'Security', 'hard', 'Exit Exam 2018 (mid semester)') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET question = EXCLUDED.question, options = EXCLUDED.options, answer = EXCLUDED.answer, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, topic = EXCLUDED.topic, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, source = EXCLUDED.source;

![NAND Gate](/assets/q100_nand_gate.png)', '["XOR", "NOR", "NAND", "AND"]', 'NAND', 'A NAND gate is drawn as a standard AND gate shape (D-shape body) with a small circle (bubble) at the output. The bubble represents inversion (NOT). So NAND = AND + NOT. NAND output is 0 only when ALL inputs are 1; otherwise it outputs 1. It is a universal gate — any logic circuit can be built using only NAND gates. NOR also has a bubble, but on an OR shape.', 'Digital Logic', 'medium', 'Exit Exam 2018 (mid semester)') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET question = EXCLUDED.question, options = EXCLUDED.options, answer = EXCLUDED.answer, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, topic = EXCLUDED.topic, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, source = EXCLUDED.source;

